<title>BELGIUM: Danish Jelved sees Germany, France on EMU target.</title>
<headline>Danish Jelved sees Germany, France on EMU target.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish Economy Minister Marianne Jelved said on Monday she was certain that Germany and France would meet the criteria for economic and monetary union.</p>
<p>Jelved, arriving at a meeting of EU finance ministers in Brussels, said both countries had put forward good and realistic convergence programmes.</p>
<p>&quot;It's a very good convergence programme for both countries and realistic,&quot; Jelved told Reuters.</p>
<p>Asked whether she believed both Germany and France would meet the EMU criteria, she said, &quot;I'm sure.&quot;</p>
<p>Jelved also said she saw no risk of EMU delay.</p>
</text>
